# TMEsim

Mechanistic ODE model of melanoma–CD8 T cell interaction, fit against the
Frangieh et al. 2021 Perturb-CITE-seq dataset.

## Setup

Create and activate the conda environment from the repository root:

    conda env create -f environment.yml
    conda activate tmesim

## Layout

    src/          shared code imported everywhere (data loading, model, plotting)
    fit/          one script per parameter fit; each writes results/params/<name>.json
    simulate/     scripts that run the fitted model
    notebooks/    exploration only; imports src, holds no reusable logic
    data/
      scp/        Single Cell Portal files (all 218,331 cells)
      paper/      supplementary tables of the paper
      digitized/  curves read off paper figures, one CSV per panel
    results/
      params/     fitted parameter values (JSON)
      figures/    figures produced by fit/ and simulate/

Folders are created when their first file is added. Run scripts from the
repository root as modules so `src` is importable, e.g. `python -m fit.kill_rate`.

## Data

Everything under `data/` is in the repository except the processed AnnData
(about 1 GB). `src.data.load_adata()` downloads it to
`data/frangieh_2021.h5ad` on first use and reuses it afterwards.

## Explore the data

    jupyter notebook notebooks/01_data_exploration.ipynb
